.TH "zelta\-failover" "8" "" "" "System Manager\(cqs Manual"
.SH NAME
\f[B]zelta failover\f[R] \- promote a backup target through a guarded
ZFS failover workflow
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]zelta failover\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] \f[I]source\f[R]
\f[I]target\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]zelta failover\f[R] composes the normal active\-passive promotion
workflow for a dataset tree.
It locks the active source, performs a final backup, syncs local ZFS
properties, and unlocks the promoted target.
.PP
The command is intended for planned promotion and controlled failback
workflows where the standby dataset tree is already maintained by
\f[B]zelta backup\f[R].
It does not make split\-brain safe by itself; operators must still
ensure only one side is active and writable.
.PP
When reciprocal \f[B]zelta policy\f[R] jobs maintain both directions,
this is the Zelta Twin pattern: an asynchronous cluster pair where
either dataset tree can become active after a guarded failover.
.PP
Lower\-level commands are available for scripts that need to perform the
workflow step by step:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]zelta lock\f[R] applies ordered readonly, canmount, unmount, and
remount operations.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]zelta backup\f[R] performs the final replication step.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]zelta propsync\f[R] replays local ZFS properties from source to
target while preserving target\-only local overrides.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]zelta unlock\f[R] reverses the lock state for the promoted dataset
tree.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[I]source\f[R]
Active dataset tree to lock and back up before promotion.
.TP
\f[I]target\f[R]
Standby dataset tree to receive the final backup and become writable.
.TP
\f[B]\-n\f[R], \f[B]\-\-dryrun\f[R], \f[B]\-\-dry\-run\f[R]
Display underlying commands without executing them.
.TP
\f[B]\-v\f[R], \f[B]\-\-verbose\f[R]
Increase verbosity.
Specify once for operational detail, twice for debug output.
.TP
\f[B]\-q\f[R], \f[B]\-\-quiet\f[R]
Decrease log output.
.SH EXAMPLES
Promote a standby service tree:
.IP
.EX
zelta failover primary.example.com:tank/service standby.example.com:tank/service
.EE
.PP
Perform the same workflow explicitly:
.IP
.EX
zelta lock primary.example.com:tank/service
zelta backup primary.example.com:tank/service standby.example.com:tank/service
zelta propsync primary.example.com:tank/service standby.example.com:tank/service
zelta unlock standby.example.com:tank/service
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, non\-zero on error.
.SH NOTES
Always verify state with \f[B]zelta match\f[R] before and after
promotion.
Do not run both sides read\-write at the same time.
